{"name":"Heart Stone","hex":"#ede3df","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"},{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/500px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten